oat “Djinn”, helmed by " [:a {:href "/athletes/63649"} "Enrique Sieburger Hadler"] ". Whiton and “Llanoria” would return in " [:a {:href "/results/9590"} "1952"] " and defend their title, although the crew members were different."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The bronze medal helmsman, Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/62362"} "Tore Holm"] ", was making his fifth Olympic appearance, having won gold medals in " [:a {:href "/results/9402"} "this event in 1932"] " and in the " [:a {:href "/results/9304"} "40 m² event in 1920"] ", and a bronze medal in the " [:a {:href "/results/9359"} "1928 8-metre class"] ". The fourth-place helmsman, " [:a {:href "/athletes/62637"} "Magnus Konow"] " of Norway, was making his sixth, and final, Olympic appearance, in an Olympic career that began in " [:a {:href "/results/9225"} "1908"] ", and saw him win gold medals in the " [:a {:href "/results/9245"} "1912 12-metre class"] " and the " [:a {:href "/results/9279"} "1920 8-metre class"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Race #1"] [:th {} "Race #2"] [:th {} "Race #3"] [:th {} "Race #4"] [:th {} "Race #5"] [:th {} "Race #6"] [:th {} "Race #7"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Llanoria"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "5,472"] [:td {} "540 (4)"] [:td {} "1,142 (1)"] [:td {} "1,142 (1)"] [:td {} "665 (3)"] [:td {} "239 (8)"] [:td {} "1,142 (1)"] [:td {} "841 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "16"} [:a {:href "/athletes/64153"} "Herman Whiton"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/62815"} "Lee Loomis"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/63053"} "Mike Mooney"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/63705"} "James Smith"] " • " [:a {